{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact teardown head 7c156465e8e10a4d00f07eabe38a9552becd4916 on builder/native-teardown-20261103, tree 94364a80, for request df2abe35 under promise b8268695 and review request 9e274aa8. This approval covers the test-fixture callback join. It changes no production code and claims no G3, O4 or Goose acceptance.\n\nScope. Main d7f1ebf7 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. Against main, the head changes three test files, packages/scope/test/session-ownership.test.ts, support/native-fixture-lifetime.ts and worker.ts, plus the note and four manifests. The commit-message check passes for all three commits. No card path changes. From the gate commit 03102b56 to the head, only the note and the gate manifest change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- release() still runs first and unchanged. It retires authority and releases every owned resource synchronously.\n- finish() then joins scheduled callbacks on each platform the fixture named, through a raw Platform handle. The handle is not the owned wrapper, so the join cannot borrow the retired owner's authority. awaitScheduledCallbacks only awaits callbacks that already exist. It runs no effect or dispatch and advances no clock.\n- The join stops at 64 rounds or 4,096 callbacks, and a bad count throws. finish() caches its promise, so repeated calls join once.\n- A fixture that declares finish \"external\" still registers no automatic hook, as before.\n- The new case holds a waitUntil callback inside the object, retires the owner, and shows that a metadata RPC answers while finish() still waits. Releasing the callback lets finish() complete. Control 06 skips the join, and the case fails at that race assertion. The control names baseline fedaa09a…, the exact native-fixture-lifetime.ts at the head, and restores it.\n- No original case, assertion or deadline changes.\n\nThe cause. I accept the qualification as the note states it. The traces show a real cleanup fault: before the change, the MCP lending owner returned with two Destination callbacks still scheduled per case, and 609 of 610 module resolutions completed, with packages/scope/test/worker.ts outstanding. After the change, finish() joins those callbacks and all 659 resolutions complete. The traces never reproduce the original whole-gate error, and archive-input.test.ts passed alone and beside a copy of itself. So this head removes one fault that fits the error; it does not prove the error gone.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit at 03102b56 reads exit 0. source-before and source-after both record tree 898c138e and a clean status, and every stage passed with no unhandled error. One pass cannot prove an intermittent race fixed: the installed-registers gate also passed without this change. If the same EnvironmentTeardownError fails a later gate, treat df2abe35's cause as incomplete and reopen it.\n\nEvidence. The four manifests hash to 85eef5b4…, 924ab973…, 74037569… and 3726e709…, and the note names all four. All 32 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 56 private files match their indexes. The first witness attempt's exit 143 stays on the record with its correction. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Cleanup ownership stays in the fixture, and the join reaches only objects the fixture named.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change is test-only.\n\nSimplification: no required change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:35a29580c5d269a1d8ba5dda1f51fb927f5d635d","binding":"assigned","head":"7c156465e8e10a4d00f07eabe38a9552becd4916","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cd460176c8fc5a7e46263e19e3d7e36961a01bf9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b8268695cf8d577acd5cb68a28a27a262dc93acd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982